^CONVERSION ERROR$
C++11 auto deduction with pointer declarators.
The declarator's pointer level is part of the deduction pattern, so
`auto *p = <T*>` deduces auto=T (p has type T*), not auto=T*.
References (auto&) are not pointer declarators and absorb the full type.
